@* Creatable tags. Type anything and press Enter or a comma: text that names a row chooses that
   row, anything else becomes a chip of its own, a duplicate is ignored, and Backspace in the
   empty box takes the last chip back. Every chip posts under "tags", exactly like a chosen row.

   The chip input carries name="tags" too, which is the no-script path: without JavaScript the
   typed "rust, go" still posts, and the server splits every "tags" value on commas, trims, and
   drops blanks and duplicates. With JavaScript the box is emptied as each chip is made. *@
<div class="w-80">
    <Field>
        <FieldLabel For="cb-creatable-input">Tags</FieldLabel>
        <Combobox Target="cb-creatable-list" Multiple Creatable>
            <ComboboxChips Name="tags">
                <ComboboxChip Value="blazor" Name="tags" Label="Blazor">Blazor</ComboboxChip>
                <ComboboxChipInput id="cb-creatable-input" name="tags"
                                   Placeholder="Add a tag…" AriaLabel="Tags" />
            </ComboboxChips>

            <ComboboxContent Id="cb-creatable-list">
                <ComboboxList>
                    <ComboboxEmpty>Press Enter to add it as a new tag.</ComboboxEmpty>
                    <ComboboxItem Value="blazor" Selected>Blazor</ComboboxItem>
                    <ComboboxItem Value="unpoly">Unpoly</ComboboxItem>
                    <ComboboxItem Value="tailwind">Tailwind</ComboboxItem>
                    <ComboboxItem Value="dotnet">.NET</ComboboxItem>
                </ComboboxList>
            </ComboboxContent>
        </Combobox>
    </Field>
</div>
